# Nano mode (sys.gammaos.minimal_boot=1) starts class main but not late_start,
# which keeps the DRM home light. On this SoC the WCN3990 Wi-Fi needs
# cnss-daemon (class late_start in init.qcom.rc) for the firmware and QMI
# side: without it the cld driver never completes its configuration, the
# HAL's driver-state write fails with EINVAL and Wi-Fi cannot be enabled.
on property:sys.gammaos.minimal_boot=1
    start cnss-daemon

# Boot chime: the sound card only exists once the ADSP has loaded its
# firmware. init.qti.kernel.rc boots the ADSP at early-boot (~10 s), the
# audio HAL (class hal) started at ~11 s and the card registered ~11.8 s,
# while the nano boot animation starts at ~6.7 s. The firmware partitions are
# mounted by the hw rc's mount_all in fs/late-fs, which runs before this block,
# so boot the ADSP here (~6.4 s); the audio HAL service is class early_hal
# (started at late-fs) and retries the sound card until it appears.
on late-fs
    exec_background u:r:vendor_qti_init_shell_bg:s0 -- /vendor/bin/init.qti.write.sh /sys/kernel/boot_adsp/boot 1
